<span id="freeTextContainer13600069482530104956">If other fantasy manga didn&apos;t already exist, this one might have felt fresh and new. The difficulty is that even the humor felt derivative of other manga stories. The characters are weird and different in some ways, but the main character is just the traditional &quot;tough, spunky and a bit stupid&quot; kid who is powerful but incompetent at the start.<br/>On the other hand, the artwork was good for the style, and the action-adventure parts were fun to read, even if they felt like a lost volume of another ser</span>
  <span id="freeText13600069482530104956" style="display:none">If other fantasy manga didn't already exist, this one might have felt fresh and new. The difficulty is that even the humor felt derivative of other manga stories. The characters are weird and different in some ways, but the main character is just the traditional "tough, spunky and a bit stupid" kid who is powerful but incompetent at the start.<br />On the other hand, the artwork was good for the style, and the action-adventure parts were fun to read, even if they felt like a lost volume of another series.<br />The main character is a young man who has, like other wizards, been infected by the monsters who are ravaging the world. Basically, anyone who survives being touched by one is infected, and comes away with some form of physical or mental mutation, but also the ability to manipulate magic. Sadly, the author didn't do arithmetic very well, or a LOT of people are stupid enough to get touched by one of these Nemeses, even though the natural reaction to them is to run far away. <br />In any case, for no good reason, there is an inquisition whose apparent job is to arrest the only people capable of fighting back against the monsters. Also, no one really knows the sources of the monsters, who apparently just fall out of the sky, at least sometimes in really big eggs.<br />Overall, the book is moderately enjoyable but forgettable. I read it when it first came out, several months ago, and then re-read it to see if my opinion had changed. It hadn't, but I couldn't remember most of what happened. For me, that is unusual, and suggests that I didn't really care what happened.<br />So, if you read Naruto or other manga for the crazy young hero, rather than for the overall story, then you might enjoy this one. He's good-hearted but deranged, and the story looks like it will lead somewhere interesting.</span>
  <a data-text-id="13600069482530104956" href="#" onclick="swapContent($(this));; return false;">...more</a>

          </span>
