  <span id="freeText5975879464579591732" style="display:none">A French manga. It’s a fairly generic shonen. The closest influence in style is probably fairy tail. Art is so-so at this point. The color work is good but the rest lacks detail. The writing is on the wordy side.<br /><br />The setting is cloud islands with little villages on them, a familiar jrpg concept. These islands are occasionally bombarded by nemeses that fall from the heavens. No one knows why. But they are dangerous and destructive. The only ones who can fight them are wizards, who are immune to nemeses but suffer from a unique affliction. The public hates the wizards almost as much as the nemeses (similar to the Witcher). There is an organization tasked with hunting down wizards called the inquisition.<br /><br />The hero, Seth, is a typical shonen protagonist. Excitable, ambitious, kind-hearted, and stupid. (An imitation Luffy, basically) He has a special ability to grasp fantasia which will one day make him supremely powerful.<br /><br />A nemesis lands near Seth and he runs out to fight it, despite his teacher, Alma, insisting that he is not ready.<br /><br />SPOILER<br /><br />A rival group of wizards, the bravetastic 4 also show up. Seth agrees to fight while they take the villagers to safety in the town bank.<br /><br />Seth wrecks half the town in his fight and fails to defeat the nemesis. He decides to flee with a child to the bank.<br /><br />However the bravetastic 4 are actually petty thieves who have robbed the townsfolk.<br /><br />The nemesis shows up at the bank and Seth finally defeats it using his special ability.<br /><br />Alma shows up and captures the bravetastic 4.<br /><br />A cleaning wizard shows up to remove the nemesis corpse.<br /><br />Seth declares that he wants to find the memeses’ nest (radiant) and destroy it once and for all.<br /><br />He leaves with the cleaning wizard to train and seek info at the wizard academy. Everyone cries.<br /><br />Seth and the cleaning wizard are intercepted by the inquisition.<br /><br />They rescue Melie and escape to the wizard academy.<br /><br />Seth impulsively signs a bad contract with the yellow cat.<br /><br />Melie’s infection involves her turning into a bitch, but Seth rolls with it, earning her esteem.<br /><br />Seth begins training with a grouchy wizard.<br /><br />The eyepatch inquisitor reports back to a grand inquisitor who believes Seth will pose a danger due to his ability and orders his capture.</span>
