  <span id="freeText3404856405036520638" style="display:none">Jumped into this one as I liked the art on the cover and what. a. discovery! Absolutely hooked by the end of the first chapter. <br /><br />First off the artwork is sublime, it's by a french artist who has captured the essence of Japanese art to a tee but also manages to add in western comic influences creating a mix of gorgeous character design and world. I didn't realise but it's a story about magic and demons. There are witches, there are wizards, there are cities floating in the skies and there are demons who rain hell down on the people below. It's an interesting premise as it's all about wizards who are the only ones who can fight and kill these 'Nemesis', yet they are constantly hounded and beaten by humans who fear their power. Some wizards use their might to rob the weak whilst others, our main character Seth, are legitimately trying to save people despite the hate they receive. <br /><br />The writing too is actually funny. There are quite a few jokes in here that land appropriately and mixed in well with the action, which there is enough off without feeling tired. By the end of the volume, you are shown and told enough to set the world of wizards alight with a character who is both instantly appealing but also newbie enough for the audience to grow with. A lot of inspiration from Naruto can be felt so if you're a fan of that, it's worth a read. </span>
