  <span id="freeText16763283238328772919" style="display:none">Wow, one of the few euro-manga I've read that feels like it's drawings could make it in one of the big shonen magazines!<br /><br />The plot setup isn't quite as polished as the art, but I am okay with some "early installment weirdness", and the premises is sound: world with magic monsters that either kill or give you an infection (magic powers + some weird curse; horns for the MC). The cursed people are feared by others. Our hero, a hotheaded and not overtly burdened by forethough boy with some unusually strong, if unpolished, magic powers sets out to learn to control his infection and find a source of these monsters. Cue music<br /><br />It's got vibes of One Piece, Fairy Tale (but less ick fanservice by far), Dragonball, I even see a hint of Ghibli bandits in the background, but it's smooth enough that it doesn't feel like any one series ripped off. Will definitely keep on with this</span>
