  <span id="freeText2990848066664450497" style="display:none">It's pretty cool to see a French comic truly embrace the Japanese manga art style, and it was the main reason I picked up Radiant in the first place... along with me ordering for a kid at my school's library. I've read a decent amount of manga over the years, and far, far more anime, and unfortunately Radiant just didn't click with me. To put it into perspective for manga fans, a lot of people describe Black Clover - one of my favorite Shounen anime/manga - as a poor man's Naruto. Radiant feels like a poor man's Black Clover, so that says a lot about it. I really, really like the art and character designs for the most part, but the story and dialouge just didn't click with me. I won't say I won't read it further, but for now, I think I'm good with Radiant for now.</span>
