<span id="freeTextContainer10761344725054471216">This is one of the better Shonens I’ve read in a while! <br/><br/>It’s genuinely funny at times, I like the characters and the art is fun. The story itself is a little confusing, there’s a lot of exposition and unfortunately, like BNHA, the bad guys are called something so on the nose: nemeses. <br/><br/>But I also have the second volume from the library so I might continue the story. I was interested in the series because it has a diverse cast from what I’ve seen online. </span>

          </span>
