  <span id="freeText15407031229882725591" style="display:none"><b>Update: THIS SERIES GETS A LOT BETTER! PLEASE KEEP READING!</b> But I'll leave my review of this particular volume below.<br /><br />I’m pretty sure this review is going to feel more like an episode of cinema sins, but here we go.<br /><br />THIS ENTIRE BOOK IS A BAD RETELLING OF DRAGONBALL WITH FAIRY TAIL AND ONE PIECE MIXED IN! What fight scenes there are were lackluster and the story dragged way too much trying to flesh out the world. Anyway, let’s begin.<br /><br /><a class="jsShowSpoiler spoilerAction">(view spoiler)</a><span class="spoilerContainer" style="display: none">[Giant monsters fall from the sky and wizards (ooh Fairy Tail) can kill them. These monsters are called Nemeses and any human who even touches one will die. Unless you happen to be the 1% that survives, gaining the ability to use magic called Fantasia and thus becoming a wizard. Great plot line right? Except that all the normal people are afraid of wizards because they wield the same power as the Nemeses. Okay, that fear is understandable. <br /><br />Enter our hero to be: Seth. He’s stupid. Like Goku stupid. He doesn’t even know what a cow is. Yes, the cows are just spotted elephant things (like the weird creatures in One Piece) but his milk still has a picture of one on the side. <br /><br />Moving on, he’s got a teacher, Alma. I like her. She at least knows what she’s doing. <br /><br />Then there are the villagers. Their first response to Alma is ‘WITCH!’ She tries to buy something and the merchant would rather destroy his entire shop than do business with her. He even offers his wife as an offering for sacrifice so Alma would leave. Note: ALL SHE DID WAS FLY IN ON A BROOM! Next, the rest of the village is chasing Seth for punching a cow and causing a stampede. When they all realize that Seth and Alma can use magic, their response is to pelt them with rocks. IF THESE WIZARDS COULD REALLY USE MAGIC POWERFUL ENOUGH TO CAUSE THAT KIND OF FEAR, THROWING ROCKS IS A REALLY STUPID IDEA.<br /><br />To sum up what happens next, a monster shows up, as do some obvious villains; Seth manages to save the day and gains the friendship of the townsfolk who are still stupid and scared of Alma.<br /><br />Next, we meet the human version of Oolong called Doc and his lovely assistant Melie who is... who am I kidding, SHE’S LAUNCH! A CHARACTER SO BAD EVEN HER OWN CREATOR FORGOT SHE EXISTED!<br /><br />In summary: THIS ENTIRE BOOK IS A BAD RETELLING OF DRAGONBALL WITH FAIRY TAIL AND ONE PIECE MIXED IN! But in the spirit of fairness, I do plan to read the next volume in hopes that it will redeem itself.  <a class="jsHideSpoiler spoilerAction">(hide spoiler)</a>]</span></span>
